data.content:
Here are the three breaking changes and fixes:

---

### 1. `ExecuteUpdateAsync` — no longer accepts expression trees

EF Core 10 added a non-expression `Func<>` overload. Your expression-tree code won't compile because the compiler now prefers the simpler overload. **Replace the entire manual expression tree with a plain lambda:**

```csharp
await context.Blogs.ExecuteUpdateAsync(s =>
{
    s.SetProperty(b => b.Views, 8);
    if (nameChanged)
    {
        s.SetProperty(b => b.Name, "foo");
    }
});
```

---

### 2. Complex type column names are now uniquified / nested paths changed

Two related changes:
- **Duplicate names get a numeric suffix** — `ShippingAddress.Street` and `BillingAddress.Street` no longer silently share one column; the second gets `Street1`.
- **Nested complex types use the full path** — `Order.Payment.BillingAddress.City` now maps to column `Payment_BillingAddress_City` instead of `BillingAddress_City`.

If you have an existing database, **pin the old column names explicitly** to avoid a breaking migration:

```csharp
// Fix duplicate-name uniquification
modelBuilder.Entity<Customer>(b =>
{
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.ShippingAddress,
        p => p.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("Street"));
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.BillingAddress,
        p => p.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("Street"));
});

// Fix nested complex type full-path naming
modelBuilder.Entity<Order>()
    .ComplexProperty(o => o.Payment)
    .ComplexProperty(p => p.BillingAddress)
    .Property(a => a.City)
    .HasColumnName("BillingAddress_City");   // old name
```

---

### 3. `IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger` — new `logCommandText` parameter

Every method gained a `string logCommandText` parameter (for redacted SQL logging). **Add it to your signatures:**

```csharp
public class MyLogger : IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger
{
    public InterceptionResult<DbDataReader> CommandReaderExecuting(
        IRelationalConnection connection,
        DbCommand command,
        DbContext context,
        Guid commandId,
        Guid connectionId,
        DateTimeOffset startTime,
        string logCommandText)          // ← new parameter
    {
        // Use logCommandText (redacted) for logging instead of command.CommandText
    }
}
```

Update **all** methods on the interface (`CommandReaderExecuted`, `CommandScalarExecuting`, etc.) the same way.
